<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Open up the home page and either log in as an exiting user, make an account or use a guest session.</li>
        <li>Either paste your code into the text box or upload a file of your choice.</li>
        <li>Click Generate Pseudocode and wait for the program to output your pseudocode.</li>
        <li>Make small edits and recompile until the logic that you're looking for is clear.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="doc-callout">Tip: Use our error catchers to fix and clean your code. Make sure to not forgot identations!</div>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>How Compilation Works</h2>
    <p>Pseudocoder converts your input into clean and straight forward pseudocode to help you with understanding the logic behind it. It is not meant to replace full language compilors but rather for support.</p>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Your input is parsed and tokenized using abstract syntax trees.</li>
        <li>The generator then cosumes these tokens and produces readable pseudocode for learning and planning.</li>
        <li>The output can be refined by recompiling or used as a reference when coding.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Best Practices</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Break large problems into smaller functions before compiling to avoid complex errors.</li>
        <li>Use consistent naming for variables so that the output stays readable.</li>
        <li>Imports and methods will not work, only input basic codes.</li>
        <li>Save and copy your code for safe measures.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li><strong>Compilation failed:</strong> Check for missing braces, invalid syntax, or wrong language.</li>
        <li><strong>Output looks wrong:</strong> Simplify input and recompile in smaller chunks.</li>
        <li><strong>No output:</strong> Email us for support. This would be an error in the backend!</li>
        <li><strong>Slow response:</strong> Reduce file size or reduce your code into smaller parts.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
    <h2>Shortcuts and Tips</h2>
    <ul class="doc-list">
        <li>Use the upload file option when working with large inputs of code.</li>
        <li>Copy the pseudocode to a safe place before making major edits.</li>
        <li>Check the FAQ for answers to common questions.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

